# Plan Implementation (Kinsenas)

When executing an approved plan (or a plan attached to the conversation), follow this order **before** marking work complete.

**Before implementation:** plans must follow [feature-planning.mdc](./feature-planning.mdc) and [testing.mdc](./testing.mdc) — impact analysis, conflict decisions, TDD todos, seeders, factories, and adjacent UI should already be listed in the plan. Major plans live in `.cursor/plans/` per [feature-plans.mdc](./feature-plans.mdc) (`YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<task-slug>-plan.md`).

## When this rule applies

### Full workflow

Breakdown file, implementation summary, and commit suggestions:

- Approved plans
- Feature rollouts
- Bug fixes that change behavior
- Migrations, auth, or deploy-impacting changes
- Inertia/React UI or admin workflow changes

### Lightweight workflow

Implementation summary only — **no breakdown file**:

- Cursor rules or agent config only
- Copy or styling with no behavior change
- Dependency bumps with no app logic change

## 1. Documentation (optional)

**Default:** do **not** create or update `docs/` unless the user explicitly asks for documentation or the plan includes a docs todo.

When docs **are** requested, follow `documentation.mdc`:

| Change type                            | Typical path                   |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Admin UI workflows, ops, internal APIs | `docs/admin/<kebab-case>.md`   |
| Member/end-user how-to                 | `docs/members/<kebab-case>.md` |
| Both audiences                         | Split into two files           |

If no doc exists for the feature, extend the closest sibling rather than inventing a new file unless the plan specifies one.

**Admin doc content rules** (strict — see `documentation.mdc`):

- Inertia admin UI paths only; no `php artisan` or shell commands in `docs/admin/` or `docs/members/`
- Never link to or mention `.cursor/` paths in published markdown
- CLI audit/deploy/test commands belong in `.cursor/breakdowns/` and implementation replies for engineers

**Kinsenas terminology:**

- **Admin** — Inertia/React app with `AppSidebar`, pages under `resources/js/pages/`
- **Member** — end-user flows (when added; today mostly dashboard and settings)

There are **no published doc URLs** yet. Reference local paths only (e.g. `docs/admin/feature-name.md`).

## 2. Plan todo alignment

If the plan has a docs todo, complete it in the same pass as code — not as a follow-up.

When updating the plan file todos, mark the docs item done only after markdown reflects the shipped behavior.

## 3. Testing (Kinsenas)

Follow [testing.mdc](./testing.mdc) — the authoritative testing standard.

### During implementation

- Write **failing tests before** production code (RED → GREEN → REFACTOR).
- Run **affected** tests during development: `php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/...` or `tests/Browser/...`.
- If impact analysis found **conflicts**, confirm user decisions are recorded in the plan `## Decisions` section before implementing.
- Before marking work complete, run **in-scope tests** per [testing.mdc](./testing.mdc) (new tests + impact-matrix regression files). Do not run the full suite unless the user asks; CI runs `composer ci:check` on pull requests.

### In breakdowns and replies

- List **suggested** test commands for manual re-run (Feature + Browser paths).
- If the user explicitly asks not to run tests in-session, skip execution but still write tests and list commands.

### Browser tests

- Use **Pest 5 browser tests** (`pestphp/pest-plugin-browser`, `tests/Browser/`) — **do not add Laravel Dusk**.
- Required for new/changed Inertia workflows per [testing.mdc](./testing.mdc).

### When browser tests are required

| Change type                   | Visual QA in breakdown | Browser test        |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------- |
| Backend-only                  | Skip                   | Feature test only   |
| New Inertia page or component | Required               | Smoke or happy path |
| New admin workflow            | Required               | Flow test           |
| Modal / confirmation UX       | Required               | Interaction test    |
| CSS-only tweak                | Required               | Optional (N/A in impact matrix) |

## 4. Kinsenas verify checklist

Include applicable items in breakdowns and Linear comments:

- `php artisan migrate` — if migrations changed
- `php artisan wayfinder:generate --no-interaction` — if routes or controllers changed (or confirm Vite Wayfinder plugin regen on dev)
- `vendor/bin/pint --dirty` — if PHP changed
- `npm run dev` or `npm run build` — if `resources/js/` changed
- Manual check in Herd: `http://financial-literacy.test`

## 5. Commit messages (suggest only)

Do **not** commit unless the user asks. At the end of plan implementation, provide suggested commits the user can copy.

### A. Application code (always when code changed)

```
Summary: <imperative verb> <what changed> (<scope if helpful>)

<body — 1–3 sentences on why, not a file list>
```

Match existing repo style: concise summary, body explains **why** and any deploy/admin action.

### B. Documentation (only if `docs/` was edited)

```
Summary: <same theme as app change, doc angle>

<body — what operators or members will find updated>
```

Remind the user they can commit code and docs separately or together.

## 6. Breakdown file (required for full workflow)

Every plan implementation, bug fix resolution, or feature rollout under the **full workflow** must create or update a breakdown in `.cursor/breakdowns/`. Breakdowns are **tracked in git** for engineering handoff.

**Breakdowns are internal.** Do not link to `.cursor/breakdowns/` from `docs/admin/` or `docs/members/`. Artisan, deploy, and test commands belong in breakdowns (and Linear deploy comments for engineers), not in operator guides.

### File location and naming

Save to `.cursor/breakdowns/` using this exact pattern:

```
YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<task-slug>-breakdown.md
```

| Part          | Rule                                                                     |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `YYYYMMDD`    | Local date when the breakdown is written                                 |
| `HHMM`        | Local 24-hour time (no colon), e.g. `1652`                               |
| `<task-slug>` | Short kebab-case label for the task (e.g. `teams-admin`, `sidebar-nav`) |
| Suffix        | Always `-breakdown.md`                                                   |

| Rule   | Detail                                                                                                                                                |
| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Create | On every full-workflow completion                                                                                                                     |
| Update | Same topic later → append a dated changelog section to the latest breakdown for that `<task-slug>`; do not create duplicate files in the same session |

### Required content

- Title and date
- Summary (what changed and why)
- Bullet changelog of user-visible/admin changes
- **Decisions** — table of retain/remove choices when conflicts were resolved (or N/A)
- Files touched (grouped by area)
- Deploy/migration steps if any (see Kinsenas verify checklist)
- **Suggested test commands** (Feature + Browser; user may run manually)
- **Visual QA** — when UI or Inertia pages changed (see template below)
- Suggested application commit (summary + body)
- Suggested doc commit if `docs/` was edited
- Linear paste block (Title, Description, Comment/instructions, Documentation paths when applicable)

### Decisions template (when conflicts were resolved)

```markdown
## Decisions

| Topic | Choice | Implication |
| ----- | ------ | ----------- |
| Income lock ceremony | Remove | Delete lock routes; update IncomePeriodTest |
```

### Visual QA template (UI or Inertia changes)

Use sidebar labels, page titles, and button text — not file paths.

```markdown
## Visual QA (manual)

**URL:** http://financial-literacy.test
**Prereqs:** `npm run dev` (or `npm run build`) if frontend changed

### Happy path

1. Log in as `<role>` (e.g. factory user from `User::factory()`)
2. Open **<Sidebar label>** → **<Page title>**
3. …specific clicks for this feature…
4. Confirm success message / updated data visible

### Checks

- [ ] No console errors (DevTools → Console)
- [ ] Sidebar active state matches current page
- [ ] Light and dark mode (if page uses `dark:`)
- [ ] Mobile width (~375px): sidebar collapses / layout usable
- [ ] Form validation errors show inline (if forms changed)

### Regression

- [ ] Login/logout still works
- [ ] …one adjacent flow…
```

### Suggested test commands template

```markdown
## Suggested tests (run manually)

# Feature tests

php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/<RelevantTest>.php

# Browser tests (when pest-plugin-browser is installed)

php artisan test --compact tests/Browser/<RelevantTest>.php

# Lint / format

vendor/bin/pint --dirty
```

Note whether a new browser test **should** be added for critical flows not yet covered.

## 7. Implementation summary (required)

End every plan implementation reply with a **changelog** the user can scan or paste elsewhere (mirror the breakdown changelog; link to the breakdown file when helpful):

```markdown
## <Short title — same theme as commit summary>

- <User-visible or admin-visible change>
- <Another concrete change>
- <Migration, config, or deploy note if any>
```

Use bullet points, not file lists. Cover behavior, admin workflow, and member UX — skip refactors that change nothing observable.

For UI changes, include one line pointing to the Visual QA steps in the breakdown.

## 8. Linear paste block (optional)

Include when the user mentions Linear, a ticket ID, or an approved plan. Omit for trivial or lightweight work.

```
Title: <same as summary title>

Description:
<2–5 sentences or bullets — what shipped and why>

Comment / instructions:
<Deploy steps, migrations, Visual QA summary, suggested test commands>

Documentation:
<Only when docs were updated — local paths>
docs/admin/<slug>.md
docs/members/<slug>.md
```

### Example

```
Title: Add team member role filter to admin teams list

Description:
Admins can filter team members by owner, admin, and member from the Teams index. Filter state persists while navigating within the admin area.

Comment / instructions:
Run `php artisan migrate` after deploy. Visual QA: Teams sidebar → filter dropdown → confirm list updates. Suggested: `php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/TeamsIndexTest.php`.

Documentation:
docs/admin/managing-teams.md
```

## 9. Response checklist

Before finishing, confirm in the reply:

- [ ] Breakdown file created or updated (or N/A — lightweight workflow)
- [ ] Decisions table included when conflicts were resolved (or N/A)
- [ ] TDD followed — failing tests before implementation (or N/A — lightweight)
- [ ] In-scope tests green before complete (or suggested commands listed if user skipped running)
- [ ] Visual QA steps included (or N/A — no UI change)
- [ ] Test commands suggested in breakdown (Feature + Browser when applicable)
- [ ] Docs updated (or N/A — not requested / no user-facing guide needed)
- [ ] Docs: no `php artisan`, shell blocks, or `.cursor/` references (per `documentation.mdc`)
- [ ] Suggested application commit summary + body
- [ ] Suggested doc commit if applicable
- [ ] Implementation summary (title + bullets)
- [ ] Linear paste block (when useful or requested)
